# Gates

Gates are a first-class deliverable — not ad-hoc shell scripts.

## Bundled policy gates

- Python modules under `src/shipgate/policy/` implementing `PolicyGate`
- Catalog tools use `module: shipgate.policy.<name>` (no bash orchestrator)
- Configs in `configs/gates/`; shared primitives in `policy/core/`
- Emit JSON findings via `write_findings_report`

## Project-local script gates

- Scaffold: `shipgate gates init <name>` → `.shipgate/gates/<name>.sh`
- Shell helpers in bundled `gates/lib.sh` (`gate_init`, `gate_fail`, `gate_finish`)
- Discovered at runtime into the `local-gates` suite
- `policy` suite = bundled policy gates; `local-gates` = project-discovered gates

## Rules

- Gates must be deterministic and scoped to the project target
- Reuse `policy/core` helpers — do not duplicate finding JSON shape
- New bundled policy gates need catalog tool YAML (`module:`) + config + `gate_json` (or dedicated) normalizer
- Do not inline Python in shell gates; do not wrap pure-Python policy modules in bash
